[{:db/id 17592186157369 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e581a350-34fb-5bb6-8fc4-e9d06576ecf2" "question-51c295b5-218d-536a-afb4-4f24a659df27"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e581a350-34fb-5bb6-8fc4-e9d06576ecf2" :question/id #uuid "e581a350-34fb-5bb6-8fc4-e9d06576ecf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-90531" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =2-{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c501e9ae-0a39-5e88-9d3f-80627d2d0978"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c501e9ae-0a39-5e88-9d3f-80627d2d0978" :answer-field/id #uuid "c501e9ae-0a39-5e88-9d3f-80627d2d0978" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e1dfce71-5ec8-5a3c-bd1e-1e6fb3662f40" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d0832666-aa34-5722-9c73-1e8c1c1870ca" "answer-e1dfce71-5ec8-5a3c-bd1e-1e6fb3662f40" "answer-dd759a9a-fce0-5c1b-a261-33cbdb2e7216" "answer-a5575a9f-2ab2-5d7f-a9f8-276caa836627" "answer-f8e19652-da47-5018-894c-72ff00f667d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0832666-aa34-5722-9c73-1e8c1c1870ca" :answer/id #uuid "d0832666-aa34-5722-9c73-1e8c1c1870ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1dfce71-5ec8-5a3c-bd1e-1e6fb3662f40" :answer/id #uuid "e1dfce71-5ec8-5a3c-bd1e-1e6fb3662f40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd759a9a-fce0-5c1b-a261-33cbdb2e7216" :answer/id #uuid "dd759a9a-fce0-5c1b-a261-33cbdb2e7216" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5575a9f-2ab2-5d7f-a9f8-276caa836627" :answer/id #uuid "a5575a9f-2ab2-5d7f-a9f8-276caa836627" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8e19652-da47-5018-894c-72ff00f667d8" :answer/id #uuid "f8e19652-da47-5018-894c-72ff00f667d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157370 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-066a3d21-35aa-5e6a-8d2f-0980dd8ef30f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-51c295b5-218d-536a-afb4-4f24a659df27" :question/id #uuid "51c295b5-218d-536a-afb4-4f24a659df27" :question/math-academy-id "q-131168" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20(x-1)}{{x}^{6}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{20(x-1)}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20x-20}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{20}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{20(x-1)}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20x-20}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{20}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{20}{3{x}^{3}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a0c7e56e-c625-533d-aa7a-794522008c4d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a0c7e56e-c625-533d-aa7a-794522008c4d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0c7e56e-c625-533d-aa7a-794522008c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dc814aab-899d-5c15-be40-875f5ab22753" :answer-field/choices ["answer-543d492f-4858-541f-821f-46b005347464" "answer-32231228-53fe-53d5-bdc4-f2108fb66469" "answer-90be949d-ed37-5555-9606-534582ba1286" "answer-0e9efdb4-7f80-5918-beaf-297fded0d1a1" "answer-dc814aab-899d-5c15-be40-875f5ab22753"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-543d492f-4858-541f-821f-46b005347464" :answer/id #uuid "543d492f-4858-541f-